    {
      "id": "seg:paragraph:discussion:0010:0005",
      "blockId": "paragraph:discussion:0010",
      "type": "sentence",
      "source": "By using a run loop or select(), results from the daemon can be processed asynchronously.",
      "normalizedSource": "By using a run loop or select(), results from the daemon can be processed asynchronously.",
      "sourceHash": "fb99db4b314fe39afcf88dfb8ae8a8631b983fba5ebcefb267db33cb46acfe65",
      "translatable": true,
      "contextBefore": "When the underlying event management subsystem (kqueue/ select/CFRunLoop etc.) indicates to the client that data is available for reading on the socket, the client should call [`DNSServiceProcessResult(_:)`](dnsserviceprocessresult(_:).md), which will extract the daemon’s reply from the socket, and pass it to the appropriate application callback.",
      "contextAfter": "Alternatively, a client can choose to fork a thread and have it loop calling “DNSServiceProcessResult(ref);” If [`DNSServiceProcessResult(_:)`](dnsserviceprocessresult(_:).md) is called when no data is available for reading on the socket, it will block until data does become available, and then process the data and return to the caller.",
      "documentTitle": "DNSServiceRefSockFD(:)",
      "framework": "Dnssd",
      "ko": "",
      "status": "failed",
      "reviewed": false,
      "locked": false
    },
    {
      "id": "seg:paragraph:discussion:0010:0006",
      "blockId": "paragraph:discussion:0010",
      "type": "sentence",
      "source": "Alternatively, a client can choose to fork a thread and have it loop calling “DNSServiceProcessResult(ref);” If [`DNSServiceProcessResult(_:)`](dnsserviceprocessresult(_:).md) is called when no data is available for reading on the socket, it will block until data does become available, and then process the data and return to the caller.",
      "normalizedSource": "Alternatively, a client can choose to fork a thread and have it loop calling “DNSServiceProcessResult(ref);” If [`DNSServiceProcessResult(_:)`](dnsserviceprocessresult(_:).md) is called when no data is available for reading on the socket, it will block until data does become available, and then process the data and return to the caller.",
      "sourceHash": "61a460fcfe0b02586cc41eefe03f7ae1a7021f910ecb34a2e1d5a0d603b37248",
      "translatable": true,
      "contextBefore": "By using a run loop or select(), results from the daemon can be processed asynchronously.",
      "contextAfter": "When data arrives on the socket, the client is responsible for calling DNSServiceProcessResult(ref) in a timely fashion – if the client allows a large backlog of data to build up the daemon may terminate the connection.",
      "documentTitle": "DNSServiceRefSockFD(:)",
      "framework": "Dnssd",
      "ko": "",
      "status": "failed",
      "reviewed": false,
